WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:24.000
It is actually not a myth to say that writing unified the Chinese cultures.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.990
There are many many
small groups of dialects in China, but we

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.420
all use this one written system which are
the characters.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.300
That makes things easier for people speaking different languages.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.000
How do they understand each other?  by  written language -which is great!

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.000
So how does Chinese work?

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.000
A mountain may look just like a mountain with a peak in the middle.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.000
And fire resembles some blazing
logs. Put them together and you get volcano.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:24.420
I know this bit is dog... So, like, my dogs are really cute, I guess?

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:42.150
Universal language schemes were
particularly popular in the 17th century.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:47.820
People would have assumed that the
origin of language theologically was in

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.710
the Garden of Eden so the whole world
would have spoken one language but then

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:58.000
with the Tower of Babel languages
were broken into a multitude of languages.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.500
Francis Bacon assumed that a language like Chinese and its writing system

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.800
would have qualified because of this special relationship between the sign and what it symbolised.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.460
Tons... How many are there Hongping?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.420
Oh I'm sorry, I don't know.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:29.980
I don't know.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.700
Obviously, it's too many.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.000
2,000?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.320
8,000?

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.300
9,000?

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.280
... A million?

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.540
Not quite, but it is is very hard to say.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.819
That dictionary has
around sixty four thousand characters.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.320
If you know five thousand characters you're doing very well.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.100
No!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.040
Oh my God!

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.420
What do you think it means?

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.360
Oh right. It's "biang"!

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.680
This one word means that noodle?!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.000
Yep, in fact...

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.500
The trouble is not just inventing one but getting people to use it.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.540
Language needs a cultural context.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.500
You cannot really just borrow or create.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.720
Every year we lose hundreds of languages from this planet

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.680
and I would fear that a universal language might lead to cultural impoverishment.

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:10.670
I use very simple "like" and "dislike" and then I design my own sometimes.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:19.589
They have to guess!

